d3d11: carry a shared surface's pixels whenever a participant wrote them

0015 moved the copy that carries a MISC_SHARED_KEYEDMUTEX surface between two
devices onto the thread that owns each side.  It kept one thing from the
original: the carry only runs when the surface has more than one participant.
"Nobody to carry to yet" reads as an obvious optimisation and it is a bug --
**the second participant opens the surface after the first has already drawn
into it**, and with that first release dropped, the opener acquires a texture
that has never been given anything and composites from it.

Word's Backstage navigation rail is what that looks like.  Its labels and
icons are rasterised (`+d2d` shows every one, with coverage), filled into the
shared atlas, and then Office copies each tile out of that atlas into the
2048x2048 texture it composites the window from.  Caught in the act:

    altars-box copy #1: src 00007B79A78D1020 2048x1280 misc 0x100
        device 00007FFFFF8816E0 shared 00007B79A7591620 gen 0 dirty 0

`gen 0` is the whole story -- the compositing device's copy of the atlas has
never been uploaded, because the renderer's release happened while it was the
only participant.  A dump of that texture at that moment is empty, 2048x1280
pixels of nothing, and so are the tiles copied out of it.

The second half is the same mistake from the other side.  Once the carry runs
on every release, a participant that only *read* the surface bumps the
generation too, which makes the other side look stale, and its next acquire
uploads over whatever it had drawn since -- losing it.  So the carry is driven
by whether this participant actually wrote: `shared_dirty`, set where a shared
texture can be written (bound as a render target, the destination of a copy or
an UpdateSubresource, a Clear, a Map for anything but reading) and cleared when
its content and the shared buffer agree.  Over-marking is harmless; it costs a
readback.

Measured, Word's start screen, distinct colours in each region, hardware GL:

                        before                after (16 starts)
    navigation rail     2, every start        287-288 in 15
    title bar           1 .. 111              111-221 in the same 15
    black bands         5 of 25 starts        1 of 16

Before this, the rail was two colours -- its background and a separator line --
in every start measured, in Excel as well as Word, under software GL as well as
hardware, with the Office UI theme forced either way, and with 0015 reverted.
After it the rail carries its six items and their icons, and the "新建"
heading, the 最近/收藏夹/与我共享 tabs, the search box and 更多模板 come back
with them.

**One start in sixteen still fails, and it fails completely** -- rail back to 2
colours, title bar to 1, the full `rows 0..46` / `cols 0..64` black band -- and
that is itself the useful part: the band and the rail go together, so they are
one fault rather than two, which nothing before this could tell.  What is left
is the case bookkeeping cannot close.  The opener can acquire the surface on
key 0 before the owner has released anything at all; on Windows it would then
see the owner's live pixels through genuinely shared storage, and here there is
nothing to give it.  Making a non-owner's first acquire wait for the owner's
first release is the obvious next move, and it is not made here: it changes
blocking behaviour on a path where a wrong guess deadlocks.

